DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("2*(x^2-2*x+4)");
$fun_1 = Formula("(3-x)^2");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-4, -1, 3, 8} U ({-6, 0, 6, 10})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-4, -1, 3, 8} U (({-6, 0, 6, 10}) U {-4, -1, 3, 8}) U {-6, 0, 6, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-4, -1, 3, 8})) U {-6, 0, 6, 10}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-4, -1, 3, 8} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-4, -1, 3, 8})) - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-4, -1, 3, 8} - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-6, 0, 6, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-4, -1, 3, 8}))))) - ((-infinity, infinity) - {-6, 0, 6, 10})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("(-infinity, 16] U (-infinity, 10] U ((-infinity, 10] - ((-infinity, infinity) - ({-10, -8, -6, -2, 3, 9})))");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("((-infinity, 16]) U (-infinity, 16]");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(-infinity, 10] U ((-infinity, 10] U (-infinity, 16] - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-10, -8, -6, -2, 3, 9} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (-infinity, 16])) U (-infinity, 10]))) U {-10, -8, -6, -2, 3, 9}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

- _For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._
- _For derivative problems, if the result is undefined, then *leave the blank empty*._

What is the value of [`10+17-10`]? [_____]{Formula('17')}
---

What is the value of [`10+9-10+18`]? [_____]{answer=>Formula('27'),width=>6}
---

[`8+5+19-2/18`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Formula('31.8888888889'),width=>5}
---

[`13*1+10*16`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>173,width=>9}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-10, -8, -6, -2, 3, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \leq 10\}`]
- [`C = \{x | x \leq 16\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B \cup (B \cap (A)) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`(C) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup (B \cup C \cap ((A \cap C) \cup B)) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-4, -1, 3, 8\}`]
- [`B = \{-6, 0, 6, 10\}`]

Compute:
- [`A \cup (B) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup ((B) \cup A) \cup B \cap (A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`(A \cap A) \cap (A \cap (B \cap A)) \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -4, -3, -8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 4, 7, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -7, 8, -1 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \left\| \vec{u} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-4, -3, -8>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<4, 7, 10>"))}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-4, -3, -8>") x Compute("<4, 7, 10>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-7, 8, -1>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 0, -6, 5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 8, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -1, -4, -8 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<0, -6, 5>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-1, -4, -8>"))}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-1, -4, -8>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-3, 8, -6>") x Compute("<0, -6, 5>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
